From 3ab8d31e74e7881f079a6ce04cf24944216835a4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 06:24:58 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Close a now-playing dashboard that stays open beside idle
 playback

A Cast receiver loops its keepalive media for as long as a dashboard is open, and each
restart of it wakes whatever is wired to the device (a bedroom amp, in one report) all night.
A now-playing dashboard is now closed, and the receiver app quit, once the device's
playback has been idle for a set time. The time is a Chromecast provider setting
(minutes, default 30, 0 keeps dashboards open). Party and quiz dashboards are left alone.
The timer counts from when playback went idle and is cancelled by anything playing.
Tests first for the timer and for how the dashboards feed it.
